A||||1||DecadenceR||E-brake||||5||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||05-31-2001||05:35 PM||||My e-brake can be lifted about 45 degrees before engaging. Once it engages that first click, it won't move any further.<BR>does this mean it's time for new cables? Or does it just need to be adjusted?<BR>And how would I go about doing this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Voytek||05-31-2001||06:23 PM||||An adjustment can be made underneath the car, between the back wheels.  There is a nut attached to a piece that connects the left and right cables together.  Tightening or loosening this nut will adjust the e-brake.  If this does not help, take the leather boot off the lever and inspect for any damage to the mechanism.  If all's OK, you need new cables.  Usually the rear left and right ones need to be replaced first (they get worn out fastest).  If that does not do the job, replace the main cable that goes inside the cab.  One of the above will fix your problem.<BR>Good luck.||||reg||1
